module Main
import Bytes

-- FFI Slice 4 Task 1 coherence, REJECT: OwnedModifierMisplaced via an
-- arrow-tail `owned`. `Bytes -> owned (Bytes -> U64)` places `owned` on the
-- (curried) return type, not a parameter head -- `classifyOwnedParams` only
-- strips `owned` from a parameter head (`argOf`), so this `owned` is left
-- standing and `translateSig` rejects it as misplaced.
--
-- Before the diagnostic-defect fix, `translateSig`'s `goT` unconditionally
-- stripped EVERY `TOwned` it saw, including this arrow-tail one, so
-- `Bytes -> owned (Bytes -> U64)` silently became `Bytes -> Bytes -> U64`
-- (arity 2) -- the misplaced `owned` had no effect and was never diagnosed,
-- it just silently reinterpreted the arrow's arity (previously pinned here as
-- a graceful `ForeignBlessedMoveOutNeedsOwned` rejection on that
-- reinterpreted arity-2 signature). This regression pin now asserts the
-- CORRECT behavior: a return-position `owned` is rejected outright, not
-- silently reinterpreted as another parameter.
foreign module Sink "wok" where
  consume "consume" : Bytes -> owned (Bytes -> U64)

main = Sink.consume (fromList [65, 66, 67]) (fromList [1, 2])
